questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an inventory service experiences race conditions and inventory drift under high concurrency. The following Spring service manages stock updates:

java
@Service
public class InventoryCache {
    private final Map<String, Integer> stockMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    @Transactional
    public void deductStock(String itemId, int amount) {
        Integer current = stockMap.get(itemId);
        if (current != null && current >= amount) {
            stockMap.put(itemId, current - amount);
        }
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an in-memory caching component causes high Garbage Collection (GC) latency and eventually crashes with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space`. Profiling reveals that millions of entries persist in the cache despite reaching its configured maximum capacity:

java
public class LruCache<K, V> extends LinkedHashMap<K, V> {
    private final int maxCapacity;

    public LruCache(int maxCapacity) {
        super(16, 0.75f, true);
        this.maxCapacity = maxCapacity;
    }
}
